\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Preference-region-aware task transfer in MPSLGP. (a) The main preference determines the transfer region $k$. The learned utility $U(r,d,k)$ estimates the usefulness of donor task $d$ to receiving task $r$ in region $k$, while $U_0$ is the fixed utility reference for local mating. (b)--(c) $S_1$ and $S_2$ represent task-specific exploration in the GP heuristic space $\mathcal  {X}$, with overlap $S_1\cap S_2$. In (b), $U(1,2,3)>U_0$ gives task~2 a larger softmax weight than the local-mating reference for task~1 in region~3; in (c), $U(1,2,1)<U_0$ favours the local reference in region~1. These comparisons modulate the budgeted mating probabilities rather than determine the mating choice. The illustrated child inherits task~1. (d) Offspring survival and improvement over a matched local baseline update the utility indexed by the inherited receiving task, donor task and preference region.}}{8}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:regional-transfer}{{4}{8}{Preference-region-aware task transfer in MPSLGP. (a) The main preference determines the transfer region $k$. The learned utility $U(r,d,k)$ estimates the usefulness of donor task $d$ to receiving task $r$ in region $k$, while $U_0$ is the fixed utility reference for local mating. (b)--(c) $S_1$ and $S_2$ represent task-specific exploration in the GP heuristic space $\mathcal {X}$, with overlap $S_1\cap S_2$. In (b), $U(1,2,3)>U_0$ gives task~2 a larger softmax weight than the local-mating reference for task~1 in region~3; in (c), $U(1,2,1)<U_0$ favours the local reference in region~1. These comparisons modulate the budgeted mating probabilities rather than determine the mating choice. The illustrated child inherits task~1. (d) Offspring survival and improvement over a matched local baseline update the utility indexed by the inherited receiving task, donor task and preference region}{figure.4}{}}
